+template0, template1, its maintenance database and this tool's own marked leftovers, and no other client session
+(BACKUP_SCRATCH_SERVER_NOT_DISPOSABLE / BACKUP_SCRATCH_SERVER_IN_USE: refused, nothing written); right before and right
+after the restore it must hold exactly those system databases and the attempt's own OID, still with no other session
+(BACKUP_SCRATCH_SERVER_CHANGED: unverified, nothing pruned). The scheduler starts that server for the night (CI: a
+container of the runner bound to 127.0.0.1) and it disappears with the runner, so a replacement could only be made by
+the night's own job and never outlives it.
